Hi,
	Just a few random thoughts I though I'd share with y'all in net-land.  Firstly, If I am correct, monsters will not go over any 'Elbereth' written, inscribed, burned into, etc. the dungeon floor.  Secondly, these messages tend to disappear over a length of time, being the bane of people stepping on them or generally just wiping them out.  Therefore, wouldnt it be prudent to:

Instead of:

what do you want to engrave on the rock Elbereth

To:

ElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElberethElbereth

That way, it would only wipe out a few of the Elbereth's.  You see my point?  Obviously this would be extremely useful for engraving with athame's but not as much as with fingers (because it tends to get wiped off faster).

What the hell is an 'athame' anyways?

Now about a new idea.  How about something that allows you to charge rings?
Something like a set of jewelers tools or somesuch?

Or something that would allow you to create potions out of water flasks.
i.e. a philosopher's stone or magic (al)chemisty kit?
It seems the logical following of the magic marker...

Anyhow, that's enough 'great' ideas for one posting.. :)

